        heading: 'Why most voice AI comparisons fail buyers',
        content: 'Most buyer research on voice AI platforms comes in one of two forms: a listicle ranking ten vendors by criteria nobody explains, or a vendor-authored comparison page that happens to declare the vendor the winner. Neither actually helps you evaluate the platform sitting in front of you, especially if it is not one of the names being discussed. What you need instead is a set of criteria you can apply to any vendor, including ones that did not exist when this was written. The five criteria below (latency, real-world accuracy, compliance, integration depth, and total cost) cover the areas where voice AI platforms differ the most and where marketing pages tend to obscure the most. For each one, we give you a specific question to ask or a test to run, because a vendor\'s claim is only useful once you have verified it yourself.',
