        content: 'Merriam-Webster defines persistence as "the action or fact of continuing to do something despite difficulty or delay in achieving success." That definition has two parts people often miss: continuing, and despite difficulty. Plenty of words describe effort. Persistence specifically describes effort that keeps going after something has already gone wrong once. It is the word for what happens after the first attempt fails, not the word for the first attempt itself.',
